## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
AMAT is a leading supplier to foundries and memory manufacturers, with significant exposure to TSMC and Samsung. Its business is highly cyclical, tied to semiconductor capital expenditure cycles. While the company benefits from secular growth in AI and advanced nodes, its revenue peaked in 2023 and declined in 2024, suggesting potential market saturation.  

Severity: MEDIUM — dependency on cyclical capex and customer concentration in volatile end-markets.  

